<%# Shown on Settings → Deploy, before a deploy Roe stopped, and when Fly's
    session ran out partway through a deploy. %>
<p>
  <% if context == :during %>
    Fly signed you out partway through, so the deploy had no permission to carry on.
  <% else %>
    Your Fly session has expired, or you haven't signed in on this computer yet.
    Deploying without one hangs with no output rather than failing, so
    <%= context == :settings ? "sign in first." : "Roe stopped before it started." %>
  <% end %>
</p>

<ol>
  <li>Open a terminal — any folder will do.</li>
  <li>Run the command below. It opens your browser.</li>
  <li>Sign in to Fly. You'll see &ldquo;Your CLI is connected now. Feel free to close this tab.&rdquo;</li>
  <li>Back in the terminal you'll see <code>successfully logged in as &lt;your email&gt;</code></li>
  <li><%= context == :settings ? "Reload this page." : "Then deploy again." %></li>
</ol>

<pre>fly auth login</pre>

<p>
  More detail:
  <a href="/documentation/roe/troubleshoot-deployment#fly-signed-out" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Troubleshooting → Deployment</a>
</p>
